<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>BhoomiCam Gidipabali places</name><Placemark><name>H Best-match hamlet</name><description>Reported site, Best match. Seven structures and terraced fields in a high basin, 4.1 km from Kilapanga. Its stream runs past Tadama. Radar here is weak, so this rests on buildings, terrain and reports.</description><Point><coordinates>84.3362,20.0028,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>1 Tadama stream</name><description>Debris stream, Strong. The radar line runs through Tadama, where rescuers found people stranded. Pale and scoured on the 1 Nov image.</description><Point><coordinates>84.353,19.9911,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2 West arm</name><description>Debris stream, Strong. Isolated patch in closed forest. Catchment under 1 sq km, too small for a river flood.</description><Point><coordinates>84.3393,19.9929,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3 South-west hill</name><description>Hill slope, Possible. Five spots on high ground beside cleared fields.</description><Point><coordinates>84.3238,19.9847,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>4 North hill</name><description>Hill slope, Possible. Three spots in a line down the slope, below a cleared area.</description><Point><coordinates>84.3508,20.0175,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>5 Stream near Balingia</name><description>Debris stream, Possible. Small stream 2.8 km south of Balingia, which was reported as hit.</description><Point><coordinates>84.3107,19.9997,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>6 South slopes</name><description>Hill slope, Weak. Small patches on steep ground.</description><Point><coordinates>84.3319,19.9709,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>7 Baiballi valley</name><description>Flood and silt, Strong. Flat valley at Baiballi. Red-brown silt on the 1 Nov image.</description><Point><coordinates>84.4023,19.9587,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>8 Side stream at Baiballi</name><description>Debris stream, Possible. Small streams joining the Baiballi valley.</description><Point><coordinates>84.4088,19.9614,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>9 North stream</name><description>Debris stream, Possible. Pale channel on the 1 Nov image with a weak radar drop. Joins the Tadama stream from the north.</description><Point><coordinates>84.3469,20.0058,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>10 Gorge stream</name><description>Debris stream, Possible. Between Tadama and Baiballi, on the same stream. Pale channel on the 1 Nov image.</description><Point><coordinates>84.3723,19.9724,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>11 South gully</name><description>Debris stream, Possible. Tiny catchment inside forest, so a river flood is unlikely.</description><Point><coordinates>84.3401,19.9699,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>12 South ridge</name><description>Hill slope, Possible. Very steep forested slope, 33 degrees, in the high susceptibility class.</description><Point><coordinates>84.3646,19.9449,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>13 Ridge near Kilapanga</name><description>Hill slope, Weak. Small patch on the ridge, 1 km from Kilapanga. Cloud on 1 Nov.</description><Point><coordinates>84.2956,20.0138,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>14 North-east tank</name><description>Flood and silt, Possible. Beside a village tank and fields. Water rise or flooded fields.</description><Point><coordinates>84.4055,20.0008,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>15 Lower valley</name><description>Flood and silt, Strong. Long flooded channel, 10 km below Tadama. Very strong radar drop.</description><Point><coordinates>84.446,19.9546,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>16 Reservoir edge</name><description>Flood and silt, Strong. Strongest drop in the study area, at the edge of a reservoir. Rising water.</description><Point><coordinates>84.4539,19.972,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>17 River bank village</name><description>Flood and silt, Strong. Flooding along the river bends beside a village.</description><Point><coordinates>84.4879,19.9612,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>18 Main river</name><description>Flood and silt, Strong. Largest flooded stretch, on the main river. Catchment over 400 sq km.</description><Point><coordinates>84.508,19.9474,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>19 Upland tank</name><description>Field or tank water, Weak. Beside a tank on the plateau. Field or tank water, probably not linked to the slide.</description><Point><coordinates>84.2672,20.0585,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Document></kml>